  "implementation": [
    "An exact sole-consumer positive U64 range comprehension -> ordered F64 row sum -> scalar extraction is composed inside the parent native numeric phase. Both legal original builder/range setup orders have an exact summary entry and a cold boundary before either executes.",
    "The native emitter reuses the maintained checked scalar-map DAG and its original branch/read/arithmetic vocabulary through a fixed stack frame. Matrix pointers and current dimensions come only from the existing admitted phase views; scalar captures come from current SSA homes. No per-element or per-fold general helper, managed row/sum value, reassociation, FMA or benchmark source rewrite is introduced.",
    "Source matrix dimensions or an exact constant cardinality provide a finite attempt envelope. Independent plain row shape parameters establish all positive admitted cardinalities. Overflow, zero, descending or out-of-envelope counts resume the original source; the native bound never truncates a range.",
    "Exact selected range, matrix read, sum and extraction factories, source schemas and current array versions are independently rederived. Complete source setup/body/header/finish/group work, logical elided constructor/output/clone/temporary/node bounds, physical coexistence probes and unspent replay compute/comparison credit remain in the phase schedule and entry admission.",
    "Common-prefix FSMs export the exact native current tag and payload at a proved reduction replay edge. Successful summary edges also feed source membership, recurrence profitability, mutation funding, scalar liveness and image fee reconstruction. Only the existing canonical runtime selects this new source-admitted fold contract; diagnostic compact calls retain their distinct supported scope.",
    "The standalone fold uses the same original shared bound and retains its original grouping frontier. IR373 separates the composed graph/metadata; Work142 funds the new native attempt and ordinary replay. Both exact Huffman work equations are unchanged."
  ],
